{"tool_name":"kc-align","contents":["galaxy","oeb","bioschemas","biotools"],"fetched_metadata":{"biotools":{"id":"kc-align","home":"https://github.com/davebx/kc-align","license":"AFL-3.0","summary":"A fast and accurate tool for performing codon-aware multiple sequence alignments. \n\nKc-Align is a codon-aware multiple aligner that uses Kalgin2 to produce in-frame gapped codon alignments for selection analysis of small genomes (mostly viral and some smaller bacterial genomes). Takes nucleotide seqeunces as inputs, converts them to their in-frame amino acid sequences, performs multiple alignment with Kalign, and then converts the alignments back to their original codon sequence while preserving the gaps. Produces three outputs: the gapped nucleotide alignments in FASTA format and in CLUSTAL format and the amino acid level alignment.\n\nKc-Align will also attempt to detect any frameshift mutations in the input reads. If a frameshift is detected, that sequence will not be included in the multiple alignment and its ID will be printed to stdout.","addition_date":"2022-06-24T09:15:31.387295Z","last_update_date":"2024-11-07T08:41:36.745350Z","tool_type":["Command-line tool"],"version":["1.0"],"accessibility":"Open access","biotools_curie":"biotools:kc-align","documentation":[{"type":["General"],"url":"https://github.com/davebx/kc-align/blob/dev/README.md"}],"edit_permission":{"type":"public"},"function":[{"cmd":"kc-align -m genome -r reference.fasta -S sequences.fasta -s 3532,3892 -e 3894,5326","input":[{"data":{"term":"DNA sequence","uri":"http://edamontology.org/data_3494"},"format":[{"term":"FASTA","uri":"http://edamontology.org/format_1929"}]}],"operation":[{"term":"Multiple sequence alignment","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_0492"}],"output":[{"data":{"term":"Nucleic acid sequence alignment","uri":"http://edamontology.org/data_1383"},"format":[{"term":"ClustalW format","uri":"http://edamontology.org/format_1982"},{"term":"FASTA","uri":"http://edamontology.org/format_1929"}]}]}],"name":"kc-align","owner":"m.bernt","topic":[{"term":"Mapping","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_0102"}]},"bioschemas":{"name":"kc-align","home":"https://bio.tools/kc-align","license":"AFL-3.0","version":"1.0","summary":"A fast and accurate tool for performing codon-aware multiple sequence alignments. \n\nKc-Align is a codon-aware multiple aligner that uses Kalgin2 to produce in-frame gapped codon alignments for selection analysis of small genomes (mostly viral and some smaller bacterial genomes). Takes nucleotide seqeunces as inputs, converts them to their in-frame amino acid sequences, performs multiple alignment with Kalign, and then converts the alignments back to their original codon sequence while preserving the gaps. Produces three outputs: the gapped nucleotide alignments in FASTA format and in CLUSTAL format and the amino acid level alignment.\n\nKc-Align will also attempt to detect any frameshift mutations in the input reads. If a frameshift is detected, that sequence will not be included in the multiple alignment and its ID will be printed to stdout.","tool_type":"sc:SoftwareApplication"},"galaxy":{"version":"@TOOL_VERSION@+galaxy@VERSION_SUFFIX@","first_commit":"2020-02-20","conda_name":"kcalign","conda_version":"1.0.2","summary":"Kc-Align custom tool","edam_operations":["Multiple sequence alignment"],"edam_topics":["Mapping"],"toolshed_categories":["Sequence Analysis"],"toolshed_id":"kc_align","users_5_years":314,"users_all_time":352,"usage_5_years":7896,"usage_all_time":8745,"bio_tools_summary":"A fast and accurate tool for performing codon-aware multiple sequence alignments. Kc-Align is a codon-aware multiple aligner that uses Kalgin2 to produce in-frame gapped codon alignments for selection analysis of small genomes (mostly viral and some smaller bacterial genomes). Takes nucleotide seqeunces as inputs, converts them to their in-frame amino acid sequences, performs multiple alignment with Kalign, and then converts the alignments